    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23269_english_2026-02-05.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-02-05-2026-02-05-0080",
    "chunk_index": 80,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "4ec2b604c41bec95cab1fbfc0a3104e9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1002,
    "chunk_text": "4. The third academic semester for students currently studying in Grade 11 was scheduled to end on 19th December, 2025. That happened and accordingly, those students had almost two months to wait for\n\nthe examination. During that period they were on study leave and had ample time to study. If we further postpone this exam, students will have to wait for a longer time to sit for the exam.\n\nAs the third semester of Grade 11 students of 2025 ended in December, 2025, enough study time has been given for them and the GCE (O/L) Exam, 2025 will be held in February, 2026. Extra study time has also been included. Therefore, we do not think there is any need to postpone the exam any further.\n\nIn the event the GCE (O/L) Exam, 2025, which is scheduled for February, 2026, is postponed, Hon. Speaker, it will affect the 2026 school examination schedule as well. So, we are trying our best to return to the normal time schedule so that the school examination timetable could take place in a regular manner."
  },
  {
