    "md5": "16d577e276421a6ed818e4d0f86ac8b9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1968,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dca \u0db4\u0dc4\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db4 \u0dc1\u0dba\u0dd3\u0dba \u0d9a \u0dba\u0dd4\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db4 \u0dc1\u0dba\u0dd3\u0dba \u0dbb\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dba\u0dba\u0dcf \u0dc4 \u0dcf\u0d82\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf) (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9c\u0bbf\u0ba4 \u0bb2\u0bb9\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bcd - \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bb2\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd, \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1 \u0bb2\u0bb5\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bb5\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 \u0bc8\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe \u0b85\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. Vijitha Herath - Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism) Hon. Speaker, the Answer to the Question raised by the Hon. Ravi Karunanayake under Standing Order No. 27(2) on 09th January, 2026 is as follows:\n\n439 440\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0da7\n\n1. Sri Lanka\u2019s plural and democratic character has been recognized by the Constitution of Sri Lanka, which predates the defeat of terrorism in 2009.\n\n2. The Inter-Ministerial Committee has met and deliberated on this matter. The Cabinet has been verbally kept informed of the deliberations, although no formal report has been submitted. The Hon. Member of Parliament may note that the purpose of the establishment of the Cabinet-appointed Ministerial Committee was to assist the Cabinet in its deliberations on the matter and not to brief Parliament.\n\n3. The sanctions imposed by the United Kingdom on certain Sri Lankan individuals are unilateral measures taken under UK domestic law. Unlike sanctions imposed by the United Nations Security Council under Chapter VII of the UN Charter, these measures are not legally binding on Sri Lanka under international law. Sri Lanka, therefore, has no obligation to recognize, enforce or cooperate with these sanctions and is not required to accept the allegations or legal conclusions on which they are based. Any legally binding decision on criminal responsibility can only be made by Sri Lankan courts or by international courts which have proper legal authority."
  },
  {
