    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "22723cb181242858de63a6aa1a52aeed",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1929,
    "chunk_text": "3. The sanctions imposed by the United Kingdom on certain Sri Lankan individuals are unilateral measures taken under UK domestic law. Unlike sanctions imposed by the United Nations Security Council under Chapter VII of the UN Charter, these measures are not legally binding on Sri Lanka under international law. Sri Lanka, therefore, has no obligation to recognize, enforce or cooperate with these sanctions and is not required to accept the allegations or legal conclusions on which they are based. Any legally binding decision on criminal responsibility can only be made by Sri Lankan courts or by international courts which have proper legal authority.\n\nPlease refer to the answer to question number 5 regarding the actions taken by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism.\n\n4. The Cabinet is fully apprised of the situation and the Government will take all measures necessary to safeguard Sri Lanka\u2019s sovereignty and territorial integrity. As stated in the answer to question number 3 above, these measures are unilateral measures taken by the UK Government under UK domestic law. They do not legally bind Sri Lanka and, in fact, we have publicly stated our disagreement with such unilateral measures.\n\n5. Following the announcement by the UK Government imposing sanctions on four individuals, three of whom were former Commanders of the armed forces, through issuance of a press release titled \u201cUK Sanctions for Human Rights Violations and Abuses during the Sri Lankan Civil War\u201d by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office - FCDO - on 24th March, 2025, I met the British High Commissioner on 26th March, 2025 and emphasized that,\n\n\uf0b7 as a Government elected by all communities of Sri Lanka, the Government was in the process of building national reconciliation and unity, which is most important in the current context;\n\n\uf0b7 the action by the UK is a \u201cbarrier to this process\u201d;"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
