    "description": "Hansard of 2026-02-06",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23270_english_2026-02-06.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-02-06-2026-02-06-0048",
    "chunk_index": 48,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "2fb06eda2f26301f49c45a6f13503f55",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2056,
    "chunk_text": "\uf0b7 as a Government elected by all communities of Sri Lanka, the Government was in the process of building national reconciliation and unity, which is most important in the current context;\n\n\uf0b7 the action by the UK is a \u201cbarrier to this process\u201d;\n\nFurther, the Government of Sri Lanka issued a Press Release on 26th March, 2025 in response, underlining that such unilateral action taken by the UK government does not assist, but serves to complicate the national reconciliation process underway in Sri Lanka. I table* the Press Release. It was also reiterated that the Government of Sri Lanka\u2019s position is that the Government is in the process of strengthening domestic mechanisms for accountability and reconciliation, and that any past human rights violations should be addressed through domestic accountability mechanisms.\n\n6. The Hon. Member of Parliament would recall that unilateral sanctions were first imposed by the USA in February, 2020 during the Government of President Gotabaya Rajapaksa. That was against General Shavendra Silva. Then, in December, 2021, travel bans were imposed by the USA on former Presidents Mahinda Rajapaksa and Gotabaya Rajapaksa. Canada, in January, 2023, also imposed sanctions on the two former\n\n441 442\n\n[\u0da7\u0dc0 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dda\u0dba \u0d9a \u0db8 \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dad\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0db4\u0dad \u0dad\u0dca\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad\u0dca. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bae\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0db4\u0db6\u0dba\u0da7\u0dcf\u0dd2\u0db8 ]6\n\nPresidents as well as Staff Sergeant Sunil Ratnayake and Navy Officer Chandana Hettiarachchi. All those sanctions were imposed for alleged human rights violations during the conflict.\n\nMost recently, in December, 2024, the USA imposed sanctions on former Ambassador to Russia Udayanga Weeratunge and ex-CEO of SriLankan Airlines, Kapila Chandrasena, for corruption-related allegations.\n\nSo, this action by the UK was not the first such action and therefore, cannot be taken in isolation or as a precedent."
  },
