    "chunk_text": "6. Taking special measures against\n\norganized crime operatives\n\n\uf0b7 Establishment of regional special\n\ncrime investigation bureaus.\n\n\uf0b7 Establishment of the Central Crime\n\nInvestigation Bureau on 04.09.2025.\n\ncriminals and their groups through registering them in the Central Crime Investigation Range and Crime Reports Division is underway.\n\n\uf0b7 Arresting organized crime groups\n\nand their main networks.\n\n\uf0b7 Providing legal assistance to expedite court actions.\n\n\uf0b7 Analysing properties, cash flow and\n\ncrime income.\n\nThis is aimed at weakening the financial capacity of criminals and combating criminal network as a long-term action.\n\n7. Curbing drug smuggling and other\n\ncrimes in prisons\n\n\uf0b7 The Special Police Task Force has\n\nbeen deployed in prisons to raid drugs and mobile phones, which are a cause for drug smuggling and other criminal offences carried out from prisons.\n\n\uf0b7 \uf054he Central Crime Investigation\n\nRange, in relation to 17 prisons in the Island, carry out a task with police officers through operations such as questioning at prisons, obtaining intelligence information and recovering telephones.\n\n8. Usage of technical appliances\n\n\uf0b7 Usage of CCTV camera systems\n\nand town observation systems.\n\n\uf0b7 Usage of electronic systems to\n\nidentify vehicle numbers.\n\n\uf0b7 Analysis of telephone data, communication and digital information.\n\nIt was easy to identify road maps, meeting places and crime plans of suspects, using the facial recognition system at Katunayake International Airport.\n\n1. Image capture 2. Face detection 3. Feature extraction 4. Comparison\n\nIt is easy to identify criminals through this new technology. The relevant data system is maintained by the Crime Report Division.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Police has currently initiated a system to curb and combat shootings and underworld activities in Sri Lanka.\n\n1017 1018\n\n[\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d86\u0db1\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0da2\u0dca\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbd \u0db8\u0dc4 \u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0d9c\u0db4\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2 18\n\n(b) (i) The Bandaragama Police Station was established on 01.01.1948, taken over by the Sri Lanka Police on 30.01.1959 and renovations were made."
