    "chunk_size_bytes": 2315,
    "chunk_text": "(i) whether he accepts that drinking water facilities should be provided to the areas of Kakkachchiwattai, Vilanthottam and Dikkodai-Dumbalai in the Porativu Pattu Divisional Secretary's Division and the Kirankulam-Tharmapuram in the Manmunai Pattu Divisional Secretary's Division of the Batticaloa District; and\n\n(b) If not, why? \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0dc0\u0ddb\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba) \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dab\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc3, \u0d89\u0daf\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dc4 \u0da2\u0dbd \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dca\u0db4\u0dcf\u0daf\u0db1 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf)\u0dcf) (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0bb5\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbe\u0bcd\u0bbe\u0bcd) \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0ba3\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0b99\u0bcd\u0bb9 - \u0bb5\u0bc0\u0b9f\u0bae\u0bc8\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1, \u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1, \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 \u0bae\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0ba8\u0bc0\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bb5\u0bb4\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd)\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Dr.) Susil Ranasinghe - Minister of Housing, Construction and Water Supply) Sir, the Answer is as follows:\n\n(a) (i) Yes. But, some villages are already covered\n\nwith pipe-borne water supply.\n\nPorativu Pattu DS Division:\n\n\u2022 At present, around 80 per cent of the\n\nKakkachiveddai village has been covered. The total number of families living in the pipe-laid area is 345 and out of that, only 196 families have obtained water connections. Others have not applied so far. Further, the balance 3.5 km pipeline has to be laid to cover the uncovered areas of that village, where only 55 families live.\n\n\u2022 Vilanthoddam: One hundred per cent of\n\nthe areas are covered with pipelines and a number of 213 connections have been given. The total number of families living in the pipe-laid area is 234 and others have not applied for water connections so far.\n\n\u2022 Thikkodai - Dumbalai: It is technically\n\nnot feasible to extend the existing pipeline. It is proposed to upgrade the upstream system by steps such as pumping and transmission main in order to extend the pipeline.\n\nManmunai Pattu DS Division:\n\n\u2022 Kirankulam - Dharmapuram: At present,\n\nthere is no pipeline and a need to extend.\n\n(ii) Steps have been taken to extend the water\n\nsupply facility to the above areas.\n\n\u2022 Kakkachiveddai Village: The balance\n\n3.50 km pipeline has to be laid to cover the uncovered areas of that village, where only 55 families lilve. The pipe laying is proposed under CEDE Project in 2026."
