    "chunk_size_bytes": 2354,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Speaker) You will be given two minutes, Hon. Ravi Karunanayake.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) But, that President\u2019s name must be revealed.\n\n(7) Does not arise, as there was no violation of the Constitution.\n\nTo manage public debt of the Government, Parliament had already passed the new Public Debt Management Act, No. 33 of 2024.\n\n(8) A Letter of Intent - LOI - requesting for an Extended Fund Facility was signed by the former President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and the Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka on 06th March, 2023. The EFF was approved by the Executive Board of the IMF on 20th March, 2023. The EFF Agreement was not submitted to the Parliament before it was approved by the IMF. The current Government had been able to amend several commitments during the fourth review of the EFF. Further negotiations are being conducted with the IMF to accommodate additional spending needs after the cyclone.\n\n1081 1082\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba\u0dda \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bc8\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bb5\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1.\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nAs soon as the Hon. President Anura Kumara Dissanayake assumed office, the Government took immediate steps to renegotiate certain terms under the third review of the programme. Consequently, at the conclusion of the Staff-level Agreement in November, 2024, several amendments were introduced to ease the burden on the general public and ensure more equitable outcomes.\n\nThe following decisions were taken to provide relief to the people based on the discussions between the Sri Lankan authorities and the IMF. Accordingly,\n\n1. Personal Income Tax Relief\n\n\u2022 The tax-free threshold for Personal Income Tax was increased from Rs. 1.2 million to Rs. 1.8 million for a year of assessment.\n\n\u2022 The tax bracket was expanded from Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 1,000,000 per year of assessment with a tax rate of 6 per cent."
