    "chunk_id": "2026-02-19-2026-02-19-0110",
    "chunk_index": 110,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a84c297ab45bb0119a88b68ef79b4cea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1530,
    "chunk_text": "This Amendment to the Judicature Act empowers our High Court with forum jurisdiction to hear and determine such offences. This is responsible governance; this is legislative maturity and this is closing the door before the tide overwhelms us. But, while we debate about the high seas, let us remember what is at stake on our own shores. Every shipment intercepted offshore represents thousands of doses of narcotics that would otherwise infiltrate our streets. Every successful prosecution should send a strong signal to international criminal networks that Sri Lanka is not a soft target and that our Island is not their hunting ground. So, every strengthened law is a shield and armour around our youth.\n\nSir, these Amendments also carry diplomatic and international dimensions. By aligning with established international norms, Sri Lanka reaffirms its commitment to cooperative maritime security and the rule-based global order. It enhances our credibility among regional partners; it strengthens the intelligence-sharing framework and it also demonstrates that we are a responsible coastal State which would not allow our waters or the waters beyond to become corridors for destruction.\n\nIn supporting these Bills, we send a message beyond this Chamber, we send out a message to drug traffickers that Sri Lanka\u2019s seas are not their sanctuary, we send out\n\na message to our law enforcement authorities that Parliament stands with them and most importantly, we send out a message to people of this nation that we are vigilant."
  },
